# MTG Card Scanner — daily data refresh.
#
# Installed to /etc/cron.d/mtg-card-scanner by install.sh. This schedules DATA
# REFRESH ONLY. Code updates stay manual (run deploy/update.sh).
#
# The schedule is in the container's local time. For Australia/Sydney (with
# daylight saving), set the container timezone explicitly:
#   timedatectl set-timezone Australia/Sydney
# or, if timedatectl is unavailable in the LXC, set TZ in the cron environment
# below. The default schedule is 03:00 daily.
#
# The refresh runs as mtgscanner, uses absolute paths, loads the same .env as
# the service, and uses flock to prevent overlapping runs. Output is logged to
# the writable application log directory (rotated by logrotate).

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin

# Uncomment to force Sydney time regardless of the container timezone:
# TZ=Australia/Sydney

# Default: daily at 03:00. install.sh rewrites this line from REFRESH_SCHEDULE
# in .env (default "0 3 * * *").
0 3 * * * mtgscanner /opt/mtg-card-scanner/deploy/refresh-data.sh >> /opt/mtg-card-scanner/data/logs/refresh.log 2>&1